{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 4, :comments ["<b>After she has been defiled.</b> By the second husband; and Scripture calls her defiled with respect to the first, for she was known by the second." "<b>And according to</b> the opinion of our Rabbis, of blessed memory, אחרי אשר הוטמאה, in its interpretation means 'and not אשר הוטמאה' — and these are two rulings. And thus our Rabbis, of blessed memory, said: אחרי אשר הוטמאה — to include the suspected wife who secluded herself, to say that a woman who committed adultery under her husband, or who secluded herself with another from the time her husband warned her — she is forbidden to return to her husband; and this is what it says: לא יוכל בעלה הראשון אשר שלחה לשוב לקחתה — 'her first husband, who sent her away, may not take her back to be his wife' — and not from the time she was defiled under him, since there are grounds for the matter in that she secluded herself after the warning."], :book :deuteronomy, :voice :rabbeinu-bahya, :lang :en, :chapter 24, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [{"versionTitle" "Sefaria community Hebrew (PD)", "language" "he"}], :timestamp "2026-07-30T13:50:43.902462654Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}